# A VPC Flow Logs v2 egress scan: 20 REJECTs from one source address inside
# five minutes, which is exactly the vpc-reject-burst-5m threshold. Each line
# also fires the stage-1 vpc-egress-rejected rule, so this file is the positive
# fixture for both stages of that signal.
#
# Lines 24-26 are REJECTs from a DIFFERENT source address. They are the window
# NEGATIVE: three is below twenty, and because the window keys on
# [tenant_id, labels.source_ip] they must not be counted towards 10.0.9.9's
# burst. Without them the key dimension is untested -- a window keyed on
# tenant_id alone would pass every other assertion in this file.
#
# Lines 27-28 are ACCEPTs: the stage-1 negative.
#
# Comment and header lines are skipped by ProjectVPCFlow and do not advance the
# record index, so the evidence refs here are #0..#24 over the data lines only.
version account-id interface-id srcaddr dstaddr srcport dstport protocol packets bytes start end action log-status
